## Firmware Architecture - STM32 ARM Cortex-M

Glob-triggered safety for Cortex-M (esp. F7 cache/DMA). Recipes: `.cursor/skills/sc-firmware/references/architecture.md`.

### Must

- Configure MPU regions before peripheral use: Flash cacheable, SRAM DMA buffers non-cacheable, SDRAM write-through (framebuffer), peripherals strongly-ordered
- Enable I-cache and D-cache after `SystemClock_Config()`, before DMA or peripheral init that uses cached memory
- **DMA source buffer**: `cache_clean()` before DMA TX
- **DMA dest buffer**: `cache_clean_invalidate()` after DMA RX, before CPU read
- Keep ISR short (< 10μs): set flag / wake task only; shared vars `volatile` + atomic or critical section
- Layer: `app/` → `hal_if/` only; `drivers/` / `bsp/` own HAL/CMSIS. Prefer LL on hot paths; wrap HAL behind `hal_if/`
- Fixed-width types (`stdint.h`); no recursion; no `malloc` after init in hot paths or ISR
- Watchdog (IWDG) enabled with kick in main loop; HardFault logs PC/LR to retained RAM when possible

### Must not

- Disable D-cache globally (`SCB_DisableDCache()`) - manage coherency per-region via MPU / clean-invalidate
- Skip cache clean/invalidate around DMA on Cortex-M7 (including ISR-touched DMA buffers)
- `printf`, `HAL_Delay`, blocking, or semaphore-take inside ISR
- Include STM32 HAL headers from `app/`; skip `hal_if/` (`app/` → `drivers/` directly)
- Edit generated `MX_*` bodies in place - wrap in BSP / `hal_if/`
- Circular includes across layers
